@comparison-numerical-v1
Feature: EN 1998 structural scene against an independent numpy implementation
  The projection of an EN 1998 document draws the seismic response: the response spectra, the lateral force
  distribution over the storeys, the accidental torsion factor and the fundamental mode shape. A second
  implementation in Python (numpy) recomputes all of them from the raw document numbers and the scene is
  compared against it. The scene itself is language-agnostic: every row below only reads committed documents
  and asserts what the canonical scene contains.

  Further specification assertions, asserted by the Rust unit tests of the crate and not by the platform adapters:
  - The spectra diagram equals the numpy spectra at every sampled period: Given the committed EN 1998 document <fixture> When the scene diagrams are projected Then the "spectra" diagram holds the elastic and design series And every sampled value equals the numpy value within 1e-6 relative Examples (3 rows: compliant-de-office, compliant-de-multipart, compliant-en-office)
  - The lateral force arrows follow F_i = F_b m_i z_i / sum(m_j z_j) times the torsion factor: Given the committed EN 1998 document compliant_de_office When the scene is projected Then each storey of "bldg-office" carries one force arrow per resisting system And each arrow magnitude equals the numpy storey force within 1e-6 relative
  - The mode overlay of every storey slab is the numpy first shear-building mode: Given the committed EN 1998 document compliant_de_office When the scene is projected Then the deformation of storey slab "bldg-office:s4" is the numpy mode value 1.0 times the amplitude And the mode period equals the numpy period within 1e-6 relative
  - Every handle round-trips the current field value at drag parameter zero: Given the committed EN 1998 document compliant_de_multipart When the handles of all entities are requested Then each handle write at s = 0 equals the stored field value
  - The projected scene is byte stable: Given the committed EN 1998 document <fixture> When the scene is projected Then the entity digest equals the committed golden Examples (3 rows: compliant-de-office, noncompliant-de-office, compliant-de-multipart)
  - Mode and phase tracks scrub the eigenmodes one layer at a time: Given a committed document whose building projects at least two eigenmode layers When the structural scene is projected Then it holds a snapping mode track with one layer keyframe per eigenmode and a looped phase track And the shear cantilever mode shape sin((2n - 1) pi z / 2H) is 1 at the roof for n = 1
  - Pushover, behaviour-factor and storey-force diagrams agree with the seismic response: Given a committed document with one building and one lateral system When the diagrams of the building are projected Then while the storey resistances are missing the pushover plateau equals the overstrength ratio times the design base shear And the target displacement is not below the elastic modal displacement and equals it for T1 not below TC And the behaviour-factor marker equals q0 times the overstrength ratio times kw, capped at the maximum of the structural type And the storey forces sum to the base shear times the torsion amplification And every diagram has a table twin and a marker bound to the base-shear check
  - The pushover diagram marks the N2 performance points of DL, SD and NC: Given a committed document whose storeys give a shear resistance When the pushover diagram of the building is projected Then the plateau is the weakest storey resistance over its shear coefficient times the base coefficient And the diagram has a yield marker and one target marker per limit state with d_t(DL) not above d_t(SD) and d_t(SD) not above d_t(NC) And the table twin has one row per system and limit state with T*, q_u, d_t and V_b
  - The storeys are coloured by the drift utilisation as a scalar field: Given a committed document whose storeys have drift checks When the structural scene is projected Then every storey has a translucent prism on the drift heat map layer with the fields drift-utilisation, drift-x and drift-y And the scene has a scalar legend for drift-utilisation
  - A tower with a bending stiffness oscillates in its first three cantilever modes: Given a committed document with a tower whose EI is given When the structural scene is projected Then three ghost members on the mode layers carry harmonic overlays with the frequency 1 / (T1 * (beta1 L / beta_n L)^2) And the overlay tip over the overlay middle equals 1 / phi_n(0.5) of the cantilever mode shape
  - Capacity-design arrows show M_Rd, V_CD and V_Rd of a ductile pier: Given a committed bridge with a pier height, a hinge moment and a shear resistance When the structural scene is projected Then each pier has a moment glyph M_Rd at its base, a shear arrow V_CD equal to the value of the pier shear check and an opposing arrow V_Rd And the arrows of M_Rd and V_Rd have handles that write the current field value at drag zero
  - Liquefaction profile, Annex F bearing surface and pile moments have table twins: Given a committed foundation with a liquefiable layer, an Annex F footing and a pile When the diagrams are projected Then the liquefaction profile shows F_L of Annex B and of Youd et al. over the depth with the required factor And the Annex F diagram shows the sections M = 0 and V = 0 with the design markers bound to V_Ed and M_Ed And the pile diagram shows the inertial moment over the depth and the kinematic moment at the interface And every diagram has a table twin
  - The diaphragm force flow shows inertia, wall shear flow and chord forces: Given a committed document with a diaphragm on a storey When the structural scene is projected Then the diaphragm is a plate on the diaphragm layer coloured by its governing check, each resisting system adds six inertia arrows of F_d / 6, five wall arrows per end of V_Ed / 5 and a chord tension and compression arrow of N_Ed, the wall arrows add up to the V_Ed of the shear check, and a thickness handle writes the current thickness at zero
  - The base shear builds up from the roof down along a time track: Given a committed building with a lateral system When the structural scene is projected Then every storey has a shear block whose width follows V_i / V_b, nine scalar fields distribution-0 to distribution-8 reveal the blocks from the roof down, a time track with nine keyframes activates them, and the diagram base-shear lists F_i and V_i with a table twin
  - The response spectrum surface is the elastic spectrum over period and damping: Given a committed building and a site with a_gR > 0 When the structural scene is projected Then a grid surface of 9 damping rows by 33 period columns has the heights S_e(T, xi) of the closed forms, a marker at T1 on the 5 % curve and a scalar legend
  - The overturning base carries the moment and two width handles: Given a committed building with storeys When the structural scene is projected Then a base plate on the overturning layer is coloured by the overturning check, a moment glyph shows M_ov of the governing system, and the handles bx and by write the base widths (the plan widths while unset)
  - Accelerogram traces are surfaces beside their building: Given a committed document with a time-history set When the structural scene is projected Then each usable record is a two-row grid surface coloured by |a| on the accelerogram layer, an unusable record is an error marker, and the diagram time-history shows the record spectra, their mean and the 90 % floor with a table twin
  - A bridge is a deck on pier and bearing entities with transverse mode ghosts: Given a committed bridge with pier and bearing rows When the structural scene is projected Then each pier is a member coloured by its flexure and shear checks with M_Rd, V_CD and V_Rd arrows and height and position grips, each bearing is a support with draggable capacity and seat dimensions, the deck oscillates in animated transverse mode ghosts on the y mode layers, and the deck mode and pier moment diagrams have table twins
  - A tank shows its wall pressure, sloshing surface and freeboard: Given a committed tank with a shell When the structural scene is projected Then a sampled line load carries the total wall pressure along the wall, a grid surface shows the sloshing wave of the first convective mode with the crest of the check, the freeboard is a dimension that drags the filling ratio, a grip drags the shell thickness, and the wall pressure diagram has a table twin
  - A tower on a foundation spring oscillates in the modes of the kernel: Given a committed tower with a bending stiffness and a rotational foundation spring When the structural scene is projected Then the ghosts oscillate at the periods of the check, the base is a spring support coloured by the interaction check with a stiffness grip, and the mode and modal force diagrams have table twins
  - A computed pier shows EI_eff over EI_gross, its moment-curvature and a reinforcement grip: Given a pier of the computed stiffness basis with a reinforcement ratio, cover, f_ck, f_yk and axial load When the structural scene is projected Then the pier is coloured by EI_eff/EI_gross of the fibre section, the declared cracked-share grip is replaced by a reinforcement ratio grip, the diagram pier-moment-curvature carries the yield and ultimate markers and the secant of slope EI_eff, and the stiffness check is listed
  - An assessed section shows its moment-curvature and the chord rotation ratio: Given an assessment with a given section, axial load, reinforcement and chord rotation demand When the structural scene is projected Then a moment-curvature diagram with a table twin carries the yield point, the ultimate point and a demand marker at the equivalent curvature tied to the chord rotation check, and the assessed member is coloured by the field theta_Ed over theta_um with a legend
  - A tie beam joins its two footings: Given the committed EN 1998 document full_showcase with a second foundation under another building and the tie beam tb-1 between them When the scene is projected Then the member tb-1 is coloured by its tie and displacement checks And a tie force arrow of N = coefficient alpha S N_Ed acts at both ends And the grips tb-1:w, tb-1:d and tb-1:u write width, depth and relativeDisplacement
  - A slope shows its slip circles and the seismic forces: Given the same document with the slope sl-1 on the soil layer l1 When the scene is projected Then the body, the given circle with the grips on circleCentreX, circleCentreZ and circleRadius, the critical circle, the horizontal pseudo-static force F_H and the vertical forces +F_V and -F_V are entities And the slope-factor diagram falls monotonically with the seismic coefficient and marks the design point bound to the slope check
  - Every check outcome is routed to its entity or the document badge: Given any committed EN 1998 document and its check report When the structural scene is projected Then each check names a drawn document row or a document-level family, and selecting the outcome frames that row
  - The spectrum diagram marks every modal period: Given a committed building with several eigenmodes When the diagrams are projected Then the design spectrum carries one marker per mode period with its effective mass share
  - The capacity design diagram shows M_Rc over M_Rb per joint against 1.3: Given a committed building with joint rows When the diagrams are projected Then every joint is a marker bound to its check at the ratio of its two resistance sums above the limit line 1.3
  - The bearing displacement diagram shows the design displacement over the period against the capacity: Given a committed bridge with a displacement capacity When the diagrams are projected Then the displacement spectrum carries the capacity as a limit line and one design marker at the bridge period
  - Checks without a physical diagram are drawn as outcome bars: Given any committed document When the diagrams are projected Then each check of a bridge, silo, tank, tower, wall, pier, bearing, joint or tie beam is drawn by exactly one of its dedicated diagram and its outcome diagram
  - Placements, soil layers and retaining walls have a grip for every numeric input: Given a committed document with placement, soil layer and retaining wall rows When the handles are listed Then every numeric field is written by a grip except the documented exemptions permeability, soil unit weight and yaw
  - An isolation system is a spring with displacement ghosts and a hysteresis loop: Given the committed EN 1998 document full_showcase with the isolation system iso-1 under the bridge br-1 When the scene and the diagrams are projected Then iso-1 is a six-component spring support coloured by its checks, a ghost stands at plus and minus d_cd, a demand dimension and a draggable capacity dimension bind d_max, and the diagram isolation-loop:iso-1 carries the loop of area E_D with the design marker bound to the displacement check at d_cd
  - A pier base is a foundation spring under its pier: Given the same document with the pier base pb-1 under the pier pier-1 When the scene and the diagrams are projected Then pb-1 is a six-component Gazetas spring support with a footing disc and a radius dimension, and the diagram pier-base:pb-1 marks the fixed-base period and the lengthened period T_ssi on the elastic displacement spectrum
  - The cyclic ratio diagram marks the liquefied layer: Given the same document with the liquefiable layer l7 under the foundation fd-3 When the diagrams are projected Then the diagram liquefaction-ratios:fd-3 shows CSR, the layer resistance and r_u over the depth, with the marker of l7 bound to its liquefaction check
